---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('brevo')!;
const b = appBySlug('justuno')!;
const path = '/compare/brevo-vs-justuno';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/brevo-vs-justuno');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/brevo-vs-justuno');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Are Brevo and Justuno substitutes?",
    "answer": "Brevo can own downstream messages while Justuno captures contacts onsite. Evaluate the handoff before replacing either tool."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is there a documented Brevo integration?",
    "answer": "Yes. Current Justuno workflow documentation describes a Brevo app connection; legacy SendinBlue promotion instructions are a different setup."
  },
  {
    "question": "What must be carried with the offer?",
    "answer": "Record the form, list, permission source and promised offer; verify the receiving workflow and avoid granting SMS permission from email capture."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do the baskets establish a winner?",
    "answer": "No. The examples are hypothetical gross profit and the acceptance exercises have not been performed."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
<a href="/compare" class="link">← Comparisons</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">{a.name} vs {b.name} for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
<p class="mt-7 text-xl">Capture offer to permission-aware Brevo handoff.</p>
<TldrBox picks={[{label:'Evaluate Brevo',tool:a.name,reason:'Confirm the Shopify account, import permissions and downstream queue.'},{label:'Evaluate Justuno',tool:b.name,reason:'Capture offer to permission-aware Brevo handoff.'}]} />
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Brevo</th><th>Justuno</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Primary check</td><td>Linked Shopify account and subscription-status reconciliation</td><td>Capture offer to permission-aware Brevo handoff</td></tr>
<tr><td>Budget</td><td>Quote PushOwl account scope and channel usage</td><td>Quote the required product, plan and operating support</td></tr>
<tr><td>Acceptance</td><td>Permission, checkout entry and waiting-send exit</td><td>Form promise, list mapping and downstream entry</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Confirm the Brevo account before importing</h2>
<p><a href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879-Brevo-PushOwl-app-for-Shopify-Connect-your-Shopify-store-with-Brevo-PushOwl">Brevo’s Shopify guide</a> now uses Brevo PushOwl. Its import warning covers overwritten contact attributes, including subscription status. Export existing suppressions and compare a small set of unsubscribed, email-only, SMS-only and unconsented records before releasing messages. Installation and a later data import are different operations.</p>
<p><a href="https://docs.pushowl.com/en/articles/14033929-understanding-the-pushowl-and-brevo-relationship">PushOwl’s account guide</a> describes linked dashboards and separate PushOwl pricing. Confirm the destination if you already have a direct Brevo account; ask support about linking rather than assuming the old account is connected. Quote the actual Shopify account scope, message volume, channel credits, automation access and support. A direct Brevo starting price is not a Shopify workflow quote. Supplier documentation checked November 25, 2026.</p><h2>Capture and sending are different jobs</h2>
<p>Evaluate Justuno when the problem is an onsite form and its offer handoff. Evaluate Brevo when the problem is receiving contacts and controlling downstream messages. They can be complementary. A captured email is not evidence of a checkout abandonment event, and an onsite coupon is not proof that a follow-up is eligible.</p>
<h2>Use the integration for your version</h2>
<p><a href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/587-syncing-brevo-to-justuno">Current Justuno documentation</a> connects the Brevo app under Account Settings, then syncs a design inside a workflow to selected lists. It supports contact creation/update and events, requires an email or phone field and excludes global/calculated attributes from its attribute pull. The <a href="https://support.justuno.com/article/1041-sendinblue-email-integration">legacy SendinBlue article</a> instead uses promotion integrations. Check which interface your account runs; do not combine those instructions.</p>
<h2>Keep the captured promise intact</h2>
<p>Proposed exercise: submit a mobile form with a named offer and email permission only. Inspect the destination list, contact attributes, event and triggered message. Record the form version, permission text, time and offered code in your operating record; do not assume every field is automatically mapped. Submit an SMS-only record and a previously unsubscribed email separately. A list selection or contact update must not silently grant another channel permission. Confirm Justuno is connected to the same Brevo destination as Shopify.</p>
<h2>Approve the offer before adding another discount</h2>
<p>The capture owner records the welcome offer, eligibility and expiry; the Brevo operator checks whether it was already used before releasing a cart code. Merchandising owns bundle stacking and B2B minimum quantities. Support handles financing, subscription cadence and gift-message questions. For size/OOS friction, offer a permitted availability alert rather than repeatedly linking an unavailable basket. For shipping shock, provide the destination quote. A returning buyer should not receive a new-customer promise merely because the form appeared again.</p>
<h2>Queue ownership after the form</h2>
<p>Replay a submission and a checkout event, then purchase while the reminder waits. Inspect whether the receiving workflow duplicates entry and whether purchase or opt-out cancels pending messages. Assign the lifecycle operator to coordinate welcome, checkout and Shopify recovery queues. During migration, pause old entry, inventory waiting sends and keep a rollback record. These are proposed checks, not performed tests or guaranteed integration behavior.</p>
<h2>Two hypothetical offer budgets</h2>
<p>A $503 basket at 56% pre-discount margin has $221.32 product cost and $281.68 gross profit. A 10% code costs $50.30 and leaves $231.38. A $792 basket at 41% margin has $467.28 product cost and $324.72 gross profit. An illustrative 18% code costs $142.56 and leaves $182.16. Neither discount is a recommended cap; the second consumes a much larger share of gross profit.</p><h2>Choose timing and measure the work</h2>
<p>These exercises are proposed, not performed results. Select timing, channel eligibility and contact frequency for your audience and account constraints; there is no universal email/SMS ladder. Validate local sending restrictions and each channel’s permission. Compare quotes using the same eligible audience, messages, implementation and staff workload. Include shipping subsidy, payment fees, returns, messaging and staff costs beyond the fixed-product-cost gross-profit examples above.</p>
<p>For an outcome experiment, size a randomized holdout for the traffic and detectable effect rather than selecting a fixed percentage. Reconcile orders across senders and report incremental profit with uncertainty; platform-attributed revenue alone does not prove recovery. Choose the setup that passes the relevant handoff checks at an acceptable operating cost.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
